{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"discontinue","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum\/discontinue","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal\/kind-swift.enum\/discontinue"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The end of a pedal line that does not include the explicit lift represented by ","type":"text"},{"code":"stop","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"case","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLPedalV4KindO11discontinueyA2EmF","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Case","role":"symbol","title":"MXLPedal.Kind.discontinue","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"discontinue","kind":"identifier"}]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal/Kind-swift.enum":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal\/kind-swift.enum","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The pedal-type simple type is used to distinguish types of pedal directions. The start value indicates the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"start of a damper pedal, while the sostenuto value indicates the start of a sostenuto pedal. The other values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be used with either the damper or sostenuto pedal. The soft pedal is not included here because there is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no special symbol or graphic used for it beyond what can be specified with words and bracket elements."}],"title":"MXLPedal.Kind","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal\/Kind-swift.enum","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPedal":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpedal","abstract":[{"text":"The pedal type represents piano pedal marks, including damper and sostenuto pedal marks. The line attribute is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"yes if pedal lines are used. The sign attribute is yes if Ped, Sost, and * signs are used. For compatibility","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with older versions, the sign attribute is yes by default if the line attribute is no, and is no by default if"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the line attribute is yes. If the sign attribute is set to yes and the type is start or sostenuto, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"abbreviated attribute is yes if the short P and S signs are used, and no if the full Ped and Sost signs are","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used. It is no by default. Otherwise the abbreviated attribute is ignored. The alignment attributes are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignored if the sign attribute is no."}],"title":"MXLPedal","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPedal","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLPedal","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{